BT /F1 12 Tf 36 700 Td (Parcel van service note. The red parcel van was in the bay for a ) Tj T* (routine stop. At the last service the odometer read 48210 km. A ) Tj T* (Quinceware filter was fitted with fresh oil, and the sump plug was ) Tj T* (wiped and put back. The next service is due at 53210 km. Coolant was ) Tj T* (topped up. There was no leak on the card. Tyre pressures were set to ) Tj T* (the door-card figures and the spare was checked for air. The cabin ) Tj T* (filter was left for the next visit. The checklist was signed in the ) Tj T* (paper book that stays in the glove box. The oil fill was checked a ) Tj T* (second time after the van sat for a few minutes, and the level sat ) Tj T* (between the marks. The sump plug washer was replaced rather than ) Tj T* (reused, and the old washer went into the parts tin on the bench. ) Tj T* (Coolant was added only to the mark on the tank, not to the brim, so ) Tj T* (heat would have room. The door-card pressures were read aloud and ) Tj T* (written on the job line before the hose came off each tyre. The spare ) Tj T* (held air on a later look and was left in its cradle. The paper book ) Tj T* (notes the filter name on its own line so the next visit can match it. ) Tj T* (The belts were looked at for cracks and left alone. A small weep at ) Tj T* (the tank cap was wiped and did not return while the van idled. The ) Tj T* (cabin filter stays on the next-visit line because the box needs a ) Tj T* (different tool than the one on the wall. Lights, horn, and the ) Tj T* (handbrake were tried in the bay before the van was driven out. The job ) Tj T* (card was clipped to the bay board and the keys were hung on the ) Tj T* (numbered hook. The red parcel van left with the paper book back in the ) Tj T* (glove box and the checklist signed on both pages. No other fluid was ) Tj T* (opened. The bay floor was wiped where the old filter had dripped, and ) Tj T* (the drip tray was emptied into the waste drum before the door was ) Tj T* (shut.) Tj ET
